## int_greenhouse__application_users

    - name: int_greenhouse__application_users
      description: Application records joined to candidate details, with referrer and prospect owner set to 'Unknown'; the user email CTE is unused.
      grain: One row per application with a matching candidate_id (inner join; duplicates propagate if multiple candidate rows match).
      source_models:
      - staging.stg_greenhouse__application
      - staging.stg_greenhouse__candidate
      business_logic: '- Read all columns from staging.stg_greenhouse__application (CTE application). - Read staging.stg_greenhouse__candidate (CTE candidate) and use only full_name and current_company. - Inner join application to candidate on candidate_id; applications without a match are excluded. - Output all application columns unchanged; NULLs are preserved. - Add candidate_full_name from candidate.full_name and candidate_company from candidate.current_company; values are passed through as-is and may be NULL. - Set referrer_name and prospect_owner_name to the constant ''Unknown'' for all rows (non-NULL, exact casing). - The intermediate.int_greenhouse__user_emails CTE is not used in the final output. - No aggregation, filtering, or de-duplication; if multiple candidate rows share the same candidate_id, application rows are duplicated. - No ordering is applied; row order is unspecified.'
      columns:
      - name: application_id
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Application identifier from application; duplicates can occur if multiple candidate rows match.
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: candidate_id
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Candidate identifier from application used for the inner join to candidate.candidate_id; may duplicate across rows.
      - name: applied_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Applied-at timestamp from application; passed through as-is; NULLs preserved.
      - name: current_stage_id
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Current stage ID from application; passed through as-is; NULLs preserved.
      - name: status
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Application status from application; passed through as-is; NULLs preserved.
      - name: last_activity_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Last activity timestamp from application; passed through as-is; NULLs preserved.
      - name: rejected_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Rejection timestamp from application; passed through as-is; NULLs preserved.
      - name: source_id
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Source identifier from application; passed through as-is; NULLs preserved.
      - name: prospect
        data_type: BOOLEAN
        description: Prospect flag from application; passed through as-is; NULLs preserved.
      - name: candidate_full_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Candidate full name from candidate.full_name after the join; may be NULL.
      - name: candidate_company
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Candidate current company from candidate.current_company after the join; may be NULL.
      - name: referrer_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Constant value 'Unknown' for all rows; non-NULL with exact casing.
      - name: prospect_owner_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Constant value 'Unknown' for all rows; non-NULL with exact casing.


## int_greenhouse__candidate_contacts

    - name: int_greenhouse__candidate_contacts
      description: Candidate contact profile with base candidate fields plus aggregated phones/emails and latest resume/LinkedIn/GitHub URLs
      grain: One row per candidate_id
      source_models:
      - staging.stg_greenhouse__candidate
      - staging.stg_greenhouse__phone_number
      - staging.stg_greenhouse__email_address
      - staging.stg_greenhouse__social_media_address
      - staging.stg_greenhouse__attachment
      business_logic: '- Start from staging.stg_greenhouse__candidate; return one row per candidate_id with all base candidate fields. - Phones: for each candidate, build values as "phone_type: phone_number" only when both parts are present; join values with ", "; keep duplicates; preserve original text; order is not specified; if none, set NULL. - Emails: for each candidate, wrap each non-null email_address in angle brackets like "<email_address>"; join with ", "; keep duplicates; preserve original text; order is not specified; if none, set NULL. - Latest resume: from attachments where type equals "resume" ignoring case, choose the row with the highest index per candidate; if multiple share the highest index, pick any; output its url as resume_url; if none, set NULL. - Latest LinkedIn: from social media URLs containing "linkedin" ignoring case, choose the row with the highest social_media_index per candidate; if tied, pick any; output its social_media_url as linkedin_url; if none, set NULL. - Latest GitHub: from social media URLs containing "github" ignoring case, choose the row with the highest social_media_index per candidate; if tied, pick any; output its social_media_url as github_url; if none, set NULL. - Left join all aggregates to the base by candidate_id; unmatched aggregates remain NULL. No final ordering is applied.'
      columns:
      - name: candidate_id
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Unique candidate identifier from stg_greenhouse__candidate; one output row per candidate_id
        tests:
        - not_null
        - unique
      - name: first_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Candidate first name passed through from stg_greenhouse__candidate
      - name: last_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Candidate last name passed through from stg_greenhouse__candidate
      - name: full_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Candidate full name passed through from stg_greenhouse__candidate
      - name: current_company
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Candidate current company passed through from stg_greenhouse__candidate
      - name: current_title
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Candidate current title passed through from stg_greenhouse__candidate
      - name: coordinator_user_id
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Greenhouse user_id of the candidate's coordinator passed through from stg_greenhouse__candidate
      - name: recruiter_user_id
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Greenhouse user_id of the candidate's recruiter passed through from stg_greenhouse__candidate
      - name: created_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Timestamp when the candidate record was created passed through from stg_greenhouse__candidate
      - name: last_updated_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Timestamp when the candidate record was last updated passed through from stg_greenhouse__candidate
      - name: last_activity_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Timestamp of the candidate's last activity passed through from stg_greenhouse__candidate
      - name: is_private
        data_type: BOOLEAN
        description: Privacy flag for the candidate passed through from stg_greenhouse__candidate
      - name: new_candidate_id
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Mapped/merged candidate identifier if applicable passed through from stg_greenhouse__candidate
      - name: phone
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: 'Comma-space joined values of ''phone_type: phone_number''; entries missing either part are excluded; duplicates kept; order not specified; NULL if none; original text preserved'
      - name: email
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Comma-space joined values like '<email_address>'; NULL emails excluded; duplicates kept; order not specified; NULL if none; original text preserved
      - name: resume_url
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: URL from the attachment with type 'resume' (case-insensitive) having the highest index per candidate; NULL if none; ties arbitrary
      - name: linkedin_url
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: URL from social media entries containing 'linkedin' (case-insensitive) with the highest social_media_index per candidate; NULL if none; ties arbitrary
      - name: github_url
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: URL from social media entries containing 'github' (case-insensitive) with the highest social_media_index per candidate; NULL if none; ties arbitrary


## int_greenhouse__candidate_tags

    - name: int_greenhouse__candidate_tags
      description: Aggregates candidate tags into a single string, counts tag associations, and flags presence of technical or experience tags.
      grain: One row per candidate_id with at least one joined tag association
      source_models:
      - staging.stg_greenhouse__candidate_tag
      - staging.stg_greenhouse__candidate
      - staging.stg_greenhouse__tag
      business_logic: '- Start from candidate-tag associations and inner join to candidate on candidate_id and to tag on tag_id. - Group by candidate_id and full_name. - tags: concatenate all non-null tag names separated by ", "; duplicates are kept; original casing and spacing are preserved; ordering is unspecified; if no non-null tag names exist in the group, the result is NULL. - tag_count: total number of joined tag associations per candidate, including rows where the tag name is NULL. - has_technical_tag: TRUE if any tag name contains "technical" when compared case-insensitively; otherwise FALSE. - has_experience_tag: TRUE if any tag name contains "experience" when compared case-insensitively; otherwise FALSE. - Due to inner joins, only candidates present in all three sources with at least one matching tag are included.'
      columns:
      - name: candidate_id
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Candidate identifier; one output row per candidate_id present after the inner joins.
        tests:
        - not_null
        - unique
      - name: full_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Full name from the candidate source paired with candidate_id; may be NULL.
      - name: tags
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Concatenated tag names separated by ', '; duplicates kept; NULL tag names skipped; ordering unspecified; NULL if no non-null tag names.
      - name: tag_count
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Total tag associations per candidate after joins, including rows where the tag name is NULL.
      - name: has_technical_tag
        data_type: BOOLEAN
        description: TRUE if any tag name includes 'technical' ignoring case; otherwise FALSE; never NULL.
      - name: has_experience_tag
        data_type: BOOLEAN
        description: TRUE if any tag name includes 'experience' ignoring case; otherwise FALSE; never NULL.


